id: pm-xjy565
title: Extend owned workspace cleanup across release gates and interruptible test runners
description: "Deliver the remaining eleven selected release and measurement entrypoints under pm-p5u6: test runner, release preparation, installed-agent acceptance, published verification, compatibility, isolated regression control, context evaluation, intent calibration, refusal closure, point-read costs and context-read costs. The runner stops its child and settles the build lease before signal cleanup. Other packed and large benchmark producers retain their separate shutdown work in the parent."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-22T09:47:18.391Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:44.130Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:42.722Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-22T10:35:42.722Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: All eleven named entrypoints register their owned roots and unregister after normal cleanup; keep-temp is preserved; actual installer refusals remove roots; test interrupts stop stage admission and release build leases; unresponsive children retain evidence; regression negative controls fail when lifecycle registration is removed
parent: pm-p5u6
resolution: "Registered owned roots in release gates, benchmarks and the test runner; interruption stops stage admission and waits for child shutdown and build-lease release, retaining roots on timeout."
expected_result: Named entrypoints clean only owned roots on supported exits while preserving keep-temp and live-child evidence.
actual_result: Real npm/Bun installer refusals and Unix runner interruptions pass; a disposable-source missing-registration mutant fails; package and compatibility acceptance pass.
